WEBVTT

00:04:28.163 --> 00:04:30.371
He was 42 years old and I was 15,

00:04:31.038 --> 00:04:33.829
my mother whispered to me to go and
say goodbye to my father before

00:04:33.829 --> 00:04:37.121
I went to school. So I put my
backpack down and walked

00:04:37.121 --> 00:04:40.288
the passage that ran through to
where the heart of our home.

00:04:40.288 --> 00:04:41.746
My father lay dying of cancer.

00:04:42.788 --> 00:04:47.121
His eyes were closed, but he knew
I was there in his presence.

00:04:47.121 --> 00:04:48.663
I had always felt safe in.

00:04:49.538 --> 00:04:53.621
I told him I loved him, said goodbye
and headed off for my day.

00:04:55.204 --> 00:04:58.871
At school, I drifted from science to
mathematics to history to biology

00:04:59.288 --> 00:05:04.621
as my father slipped from the world from
May to July to September to November.